# PAM configuration for the irontile lock screen, as Arch arranges it.
#
# Installed as /etc/pam.d/irontile-lock.
#
# Both groups, not just `auth`. The lockers this replaces ship `auth include
# login` alone, which works for them because they only ever call
# pam_authenticate. irontile-lock also calls pam_acct_mgmt, so that a correct
# password on an expired or administratively locked account is still refused --
# and a service with no `account` group falls through to /etc/pam.d/other, which
# denies everything. The symptom is the right password being rejected forever.
#
# One file per distribution rather than one clever file for all of them: the
# stack a lock screen should defer to is named differently everywhere, and
# guessing wrong here means an account that cannot be unlocked.
auth    include login
account include login
